     ///   was cancelled or otherwise not successful.
     /// * `seat` - The seat on which the DnD action was finished.
     fn dropped(&mut self, target: Option<WlSurface>, validated: bool, seat: Seat<Self>) {}
+
+    /// Whether releasing this drag reports `wl_data_source.dnd_drop_performed`
+    /// to `source` even when no target accepted it.
+    ///
+    /// Asked once per drag, on a release that was not cancelled, with the source
+    /// still alive. When `true`, the source hears `dnd_drop_performed` before the
+    /// target hears `wl_data_device.drop`, and still hears `cancelled` afterwards
+    /// if no target accepted (Mutter's drag_grab_release for a drag that moves a
+    /// toplevel, xdg_toplevel_drag_v1). The default keeps the upstream behaviour.
+    fn drop_performed_without_target(&mut self, source: &WlDataSource, seat: Seat<Self>) -> bool {
+        false
+    }
